## Overview

`MapMenu` is a controlled Google Maps location dialog: full-screen on mobile and up to 840px on desktop. It includes search, floating suggestions, optional browser-location actions and explicit confirmation. Map rendering is internal; there is no separate map component to install.

Install with `bunx shadcn@latest add @krak-stack/map-menu`, or import from `@krak-stack/registry/map-menu` when using the npm package.

## Point selection

```tsx
import { MapMenu, MapMenuMode } from "@/components/ui/map-menu";

<MapMenu
  mode={MapMenuMode.Point}
  apiKey={browserKey}
  open={open}
  onOpenChange={setOpen}
  input={input}
  onInputChange={setInput}
  selectedLocation={selected}
  suggestions={suggestions}
  onSelectLocation={setSelected}
  onConfirm={({ location }) => saveLocation(location)}
/>
```

`MapMenuMode.Point` shows only a pinpoint, centered at street-level zoom. It hides the radius dropdown, circle, radius hint and selected-area control. Do not pass radius props. Confirmation receives only `{ location }`.

## Radius selection

Use `mode={MapMenuMode.Radius}` or omit `mode` to retain the default radius behavior. Supply `radiusKm` and `onRadiusChange`. Confirmation receives `{ location, radiusKm }`. Optional `radiusOptions` overrides the default 1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 40, 60, 80, 100, 250 and 500 km presets.

```tsx
<MapMenu
  mode={MapMenuMode.Radius}
  apiKey={browserKey}
  open={open}
  onOpenChange={setOpen}
  input={input}
  onInputChange={setInput}
  selectedLocation={selected}
  suggestions={suggestions}
  onSelectLocation={setSelected}
  radiusKm={radiusKm}
  onRadiusChange={setRadiusKm}
  onConfirm={({ location, radiusKm }) => saveSearchArea(location, radiusKm)}
/>
```

The complete radius is fitted after location/radius changes and actual container resizes. Manual zoom remains until these changes or the selected-area action.

## Host responsibilities

Each `MapMenuLocation` has `id`, `label` and `center: { lat, lng }`, with optional `title` and `details`. The host owns lookup, debounce, stale-result handling, location acquisition, drafts and persistence. Restore confirmed drafts on reopening after Cancel. Selecting a suggestion does not save it. Confirmation requires the selected label to match the input; `onConfirm` is awaited before closing. Reject failed saves to keep the menu open with retry feedback. Pending confirmation blocks duplicate actions and closing.

Pass `onUseCurrentLocation` and `locating` for the optional browser-location action. The component never asks for permission or infers provenance. Pass `provenance="ip"` or `"browser"` only for an acquired source, and clear it after manual selection. `loadingSuggestions`, `suggestionsError` and `error` expose host-owned provider states. No geocoding provider, country restriction, IP service or server secret is included.

Use a referrer-restricted browser key with Maps JavaScript API enabled. Instances share script loading and should use the same key. Loading and error states are localized; Google attribution, billing and terms remain applicable.

## Localization and styling

Locale comes from `KrakstackProvider` or `locale`. English/French defaults are included; `messages` overrides use exact locale, base language and English fallback. `className`, `confirmClassName`, `overlayColor` and `map-menu*` data slots support host styling. Keep 44px camera controls, visible keyboard focus and Google attribution.

## Migration

`MapMenu` replaces `GoogleMapPicker` and the standalone `GoogleMap` registry/package entries without aliases. Replace old imports with `map-menu`, rename picker types to `MapMenuLocation`, `MapMenuPoint`, `MapMenuMessages` and `MapMenuProps`, and use `mapMenuRadiiKm` for presets. Update styling selectors to `map-menu*`. The renderer is an internal implementation detail.

## Français

`MapMenu` remplace les anciens composants de carte. `MapMenuMode.Point` affiche uniquement une épingle, sans cercle, filtre ni indication de rayon ; la confirmation reçoit uniquement `{ location }`. `MapMenuMode.Radius`, utilisé par défaut, conserve le choix du rayon et la confirmation `{ location, radiusKm }`. L’application reste responsable des recherches, de la localisation, des brouillons et de l’enregistrement. Les libellés anglais et français sont intégrés et personnalisables.
